// `$^+` over elements with no natural order between them, uncaught: a runtime
// error, its guidance on the next line, after the output the program had
// already written (GLB-152, decision D-08 of v0.0.12). It used to return the
// array untouched, with no error. The caught forms are in
// `collections/sort_orden_natural.zy`; this one is what `messages/reach.py`
// can see, because it reads the diagnostic as the CLI prints it.
>> "antes" ¶
>> [[2, 0], [1, 5]] $^+ ¶
>> "después" ¶
